# Goal Description
This is a comprehensive, production-ready implementation plan for the **Campus Chat, Group Chat, Hall of Fame Stories, and Activity Feed**. It outlines the normalized database schema, scalability implementations, breaking changes, migration strategy, security risks, and technical requirements needed for an enterprise-grade experience (WhatsApp/Discord/Instagram style features).

## Architecture Review
The proposed features require scaling heavily on real-time infrastructure. Currently, `institute1` relies on Supabase for the database layer. 
- Real-time changes, Typing indicators, and Presence (online/offline) will run heavily on **Supabase Realtime (Channels and Presence)**.
- Virtualization (e.g. `react-virtuoso`) will be mandatory for the chat frontend to handle thousands of messages gracefully without layout shifts.
- Caching will be handled by React Query / Next.js Server Actions with optimistic state updates to ensure zero UI lag.
- Normalized data will ensure that queries scaling up to 10k+ students won't cause table locking or N+1 fetch bottlenecks.

